DESCRIPTION:TUESDAY NIGHTS: RECREATIONAL LEAGUE\n*There is one week (11/11
 ) where games will be on a Wednesday instead!\n\nWelcome to our new Tuesda
 y Night Recreational Indoor Volleyball League\, this is a Recreational lea
 gue for players of the following skill levels:\n\nC – Lower Intermediate
 . Improving players who inconsistently perform 3 hits and can't spike with
  power.\nD – Novice / Beginner. Recreational players who are learning th
 e rules and basic skills of the game.\n\nIf you're a competitive player pl
 ease register for our Thursday or Friday night leagues. \n\nOUT Sports Le
 ague provides fun\, recreation\, and social sports league to Central Flori
 da's LGBTQ+ community. Our Indoor Volleyball league is designed to be incl
 usive of people of skill levels and backgrounds. All of our leagues offer 
 a great opportunity to meet other people in our community in a fun\, frien
 dly\, and accepting atmosphere. Following the games we'll go to District D
 ive where you'll get a FREE DRINK ticket every week. This season is sponso
 red by Pineapple Healthcare.\n\nCreate a TEAM! On Wednesdays you can becom
 e a TEAM CAPTAIN and have your players register as TEAM PLAYERS. Please no
 te our leagues have a fixed capacity of 100 players\, if your team is inco
 mplete when registration closes or capacity is reached the league will add
  free agents to your team.\n\nDon't have a Team? Register as a FREE AGENT 
 and we will place you on a team. Free agents can also name a FRIEND(S) tha
 t they want to play with and the league will place you together.\n\n❤️
  🧡 💛 💚 💙 💜🖤\n\nLEAGUE INFORMATION\n\n8 Week Indoor Volle
 yball Season\nTuesdays from October 20 - December 15\nWeek 4 games will ta
 ke place on Wednesday\, November 11\nMatches will start at 6:20\, 7:10 an
 d 8:00pm\n\n- Players must be Beginner\, Novice or Lower Intermediate Skil
 l Levels (C/D).\n- 10 Teams Maximum. Recreational Teams must have 9 playe
 rs.\n- 6v6 matches with standard rotating rules\, no libero players and ra
 lly scoring.\n- Games are to 21 (win by 2 or first to 25). Always play all
  3 games.\n- All games are refereed. Each team is required to contribute l
 ine judges.\n\nGames are played at:\nDr James R Smith Center\n1723 Bruton 
 Blvd\, Orlando\, FL 32805\n\nWeekly after parties at:\nDistrict Dive\n2401
  E South St\, Orlando\, FL 32803\n\nREGISTRATION INFORMATION\n\n$70 per Pl
 ayer\nLeague Fee Covers - T-Shirt\, Fields\, Equipment\, Umpires\, Photos
 \, Awards\, and Weekly After Party!\n\nTEAM CAPTAIN* - Create a team of 9+
  and invite your friends!\nTEAM PLAYER - Join an existing team (please onl
 y join if invited to a team)\nFREE AGENT - Don't have a team? No problem! 
 Register without a team and you can list friends you want to play with. Wh
 en league registration closes you will placed on a team.\n\nWant to play w
 ith a few friends?\nIf you have a buddy or a small group of friends who wa
 nt to play together you can all register as Free Agents. During registrati
 on you will be prompted to list player(s) that you'd like to play with. Ev
 eryone should register separately and the league will then place you and y
 our friends together on a team.\n\n* Please note the league has a fixed ca
 pacity of 90 players\, if your team is incomplete when registration closes
  or capacity is reached the league will add free agents to your team.\n\nF
 AQ\n\nI don't have a team\, can I still play?\nYes\, register as an Indivi
 dual and we will place you with a team.\n\nI will miss a few weeks\, can I
  still play?\nYes\, all teams have extra players on them just in case you'
 re absent on a given week. Teams can also use substitute players.\n\nHow d
 o I make sure my friend and I play on the same team?\nDuring registration 
 there is a field where you can list the friend(s) you want to play with an
 d the league will place you together.\n\nI don't know how to play or don't
  think I'll be very good\, should I play?\nYes\, join our Wednesday or Fri
 day Night leagues aimed at new and developing players and you will learn 
 the basics in a fun\, encouraging environment.\n\nI'm not LGBTQ+\, can I s
 till play?\nYes\, we are accepting to all people as long as you consider y
 ourself an ally to our community.\n\nMore info: https://outsportsleague.le
 agueapps.com/leagues/volleyball-(indoor)/5151697-tuedays---recreational-cd
LOCATION:Dr. James R. Smith Center
URL:https://outsportsleague.leagueapps.com/leagues/volleyball-(indoor)/515
