BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[Out Sports League] Thursdays - Competitive (A/B)
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261001T182000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261001T210000
UID:Out_Sports_League-Thursdays_-_Competitive_(A/B)-2026-10-01T18:20:00
DESCRIPTION:!!! THIS LEAGUE IS SOLD OUT !!!\n\nYou may register for the 
 waiting list\, or check out our DRAFT FRIDAY League.\n\nTHURSDAY NIGHTS: C
 OMPETITIVE LEAGUE\nWelcome to our new Thursday Night Competitive Indoor Vo
 lleyball League\, this is a Competitive league for players of the followin
 g skill levels:\n\nA – Advanced. Experienced and competitive players who
  execute plays consistently at a high level.\nB – Upper Intermediate. Ab
 ove average players who can bump\, set and spike consistently..\n\nIf you'
 re a recreational or beginning player please register for our Wednesday o
 r Friday night leagues.\n\nOUT Sports League provides fun\, recreation\, a
 nd social sports league to Central Florida's LGBTQ+ community. Our Indoor 
 Volleyball league is designed to be inclusive of people of skill levels an
 d backgrounds. All of our leagues offer a great opportunity to meet other 
 people in our community in a fun\, friendly\, and accepting atmosphere. Fo
 llowing the games we'll go to District Dive where you'll get a FREE DRINK 
 ticket every week. This season is sponsored by Pineapple Healthcare.\n\nCr
 eate a TEAM! On Thursdays you can become a TEAM CAPTAIN and have your play
 ers register as TEAM PLAYERS. Please note our leagues have a fixed capacit
 y of 96 players\, if your team is incomplete when registration closes or c
 apacity is reached the league will add free agents to your team.\n\nDon't 
 have a Team? Register as a FREE AGENT and we will place you on a team. Fre
 e agents can also name a FRIEND(S) that they want to play with and the lea
 gue will place you together.\n\n❤️ 🧡 💛 💚 💙 💜🖤\n\nLEA
 GUE INFORMATION\n\n8 Week Indoor Volleyball Season\nThursdays from October
  1 - November 19\nMatches will start at 6:20\, 7:10 and 8:00pm\n\n- Player
 s must be Advanced or Upper Intermediate Skill Levels (A/B).\n- 12 Teams M
 aximum. Competitive Teams must have 8 players.\n- 6v6 matches with standar
 d rotating rules\, no libero players and rally scoring.\n- Games are to 21
  (win by 2 or first to 25). Always play all 3 games.\n- All games are refe
 reed. Each team is required to contribute line judges.\n\nGames are played
  at:\nDover Shores Neighborhood Center\n1400 Gaston Foster Rd\, Orlando\,
  FL 32812\n\nWeekly after parties at:\nDistrict Dive\n2401 E South St\, Or
 lando\, FL 32803\n\nREGISTRATION INFORMATION\n\n$70 per Player\nLeague Fee
  Covers - T-Shirt\, Fields\, Equipment\, Umpires\, Photos\, Awards\, and W
 eekly After Party!\n\nTEAM CAPTAIN* - Create a team of 8+ and invite your 
 friends!\nTEAM PLAYER - Join an existing team (please only join if invited
  to a team)\nFREE AGENT - Don't have a team? No problem! Register without 
 a team and you can list friends you want to play with. When league registr
 ation closes you will placed on a team.\n\nWant to play with a few friends
 ?\nIf you have a buddy or a small group of friends who want to play togeth
 er you can all register as Free Agents. During registration you will be pr
 ompted to list player(s) that you'd like to play with. Everyone should reg
 ister separately and the league will then place you and your friends toget
 her on a team.\n\n* Please note the league has a fixed capacity of 96 play
 ers\, if your team is incomplete when registration closes or capacity is r
 eached the league will add free agents to your team.\n\nFAQ\n\nI don't hav
 e a team\, can I still play?\nYes\, register as an Individual and we will 
 place you with a team.\n\nI will miss a few weeks\, can I still play?\nYes
 \, all teams have extra players on them just in case you're absent on a gi
 ven week. Teams can also use substitute players.\n\nHow do I make sure my 
 friend and I play on the same team?\nDuring registration there is a field 
 where you can list the friend(s) you want to play with and the league will
  place you together.\n\nI don't know how to play or don't think I'll be ve
 ry good\, should I play?\nYes\, join our Wednesday or Friday Night leagues
  aimed at new and developing players and you will learn the basics in a fu
 n\, encouraging environment.\n\nI'm not LGBTQ+\, can I still play?\nYes\, 
 we are accepting to all people as long as you consider yourself an ally to
  our community.\n\nMore info: https://outsportsleague.leagueapps.com/leagu
 es/volleyball-(indoor)/5151698-thursdays---competitive-ab
LOCATION:Dover Shores Community Center
URL:https://outsportsleague.leagueapps.com/leagues/volleyball-(indoor)/515
 1698-thursdays---competitive-ab
END:VEVENT
