BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[Out Sports League] Fridays - Draft/REMIX League (A/B/C/D)
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261002T182000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261002T210000
UID:Out_Sports_League-Fridays_-_Draft/REMIX_League_(A/B/C/D)-2026-10-02T18
 :20:00
DESCRIPTION:~~ LEAGUE IS SOLD OUT ~~\n\nFRIDAY NIGHTS: DRAFT/REMIX LEAGUE
 \nWelcome to our new Friday Night Draft Indoor Volleyball League\, this le
 ague will contain 2 divisions containing of players of the following skill
  levels:\n\nCOMPETITIVE DIVISION:\nA – Advanced. Experienced and competi
 tive players who execute plays consistently at a high level.\nB – Upper 
 Intermediate. Above average players who can bump\, set and spike consisten
 tly.\n\nRECREATIONAL DIVISION:\nC – Lower Intermediate. Improving player
 s who inconsistently perform 3 hits and can't spike with power.\nD – Nov
 ice / Beginner. Recreational players who are learning the rules and basic 
 skills of the game.\n\nOUT Sports League provides fun\, recreation\, and s
 ocial sports league to Central Florida's LGBTQ+ community. Our Indoor Voll
 eyball league is designed to be inclusive of people of skill levels and ba
 ckgrounds. We offer a Social Division (for beginners or players interested
  in a relaxed\, fun atmosphere)\, and a Competitive Divisions (only player
 s with prior indoor volleyball experience who are secure in the rules are 
 encouraged to play in the competitive division). All of our leagues offer 
 a great opportunity to meet other people in our community in a fun\, frien
 dly\, and accepting atmosphere. Following the games we'll go to District D
 ive where you'll get a FREE DRINK ticket every week.\n\nThis is a Draft/Re
 mix League where all players register as an INDIVIDUAL. All players may na
 me one (1) other player during registration that they'd like to be placed 
 on a team with. Teams will be created by a Captain's Draft or by the Leagu
 e.\n\n❤️ 🧡 💛 💚 💙 💜🖤\n\nLEAGUE INFORMATION\n\n8 Week 
 Indoor Volleyball Season\nFridays from October 2 - December 4th\n  - No G
 ames November 6th\nCompetitive (A/B) and Recreational (C/D) Divisions\nMat
 ches will start at 6:20\, 7:10 and 8:00pm\n\n- 12 Teams Maximum with divis
 ions determined by registration\n- Recreational Teams will have 9 players
 \, Competitive Teams will have 8 players.\n- 6v6 matches with standard rot
 ating rules\, no libero players and rally scoring\n- Games are to 21 (win 
 by 2 or first to 25). Always play all 3 games.\n- All games are refereed. 
 Each team is required to contribute line judges.\n\nGames are played at:\n
 Dover Shores Neighborhood Center\n1400 Gaston Foster Rd\, Orlando\, FL 328
 12\n\nWeekly after parties at:\nDistrict Dive\n2401 E South St\, Orlando\,
  FL 32803\n\nREGISTRATION INFORMATION\n\n$70 per Player\nLeague Fee Covers
  - T-Shirt\, Fields\, Equipment\, Umpires\, Photos\, Awards\, and Weekly A
 fter Party!\n\nINDIVIDUAL - All players register as an Individual. When l
 eague registration closes you will placed on a team.\n\nWant to play with 
 a friend?\nIn a Draft/Remix Season players are permitted to list one (1) o
 ther player that they'd like to be placed on a team with. Please make sure
  you and your friend list each other when prompted during registration. C
 hains of friends are not permitted.\n\nFAQ\n\nI don't have a team\, can I 
 still play?\nYes\, register as an Individual and we will place you with a 
